    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` field on the owner response: **true when more than 80 owners have already been registered on the current business day, otherwise false**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerRegistrations.java`** (new) \u2014 a shared helper that counts owners whose `registrationDate` falls on the current business day (reusing `BusinessDay.rollForward`, the same accumulation path as `CheckDailyOwnerLimit`) and exposes `bulkSignupWarning(...)` as `count > 80`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 marked the new computed field `ignore = true` since it has no source on the `Owner` entity.\n\n4. **Responders** (`RespondWithOwner` for GET, `RespondWithOwnerCreated` for POST, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated` for PUT) \u2014 inject `OwnerRepository` and set the flag on the DTO after mapping.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` test passes: a fresh create followed by `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `bulkSignupWarning: false` (only one owner registered today), and the `>80` branch shares the same daily-count logic as the existing daily-limit rule.",
